      "title": "Lifecycle Methods In Action",
      "sourceHash": "72e684a01c6d2f336fbe189c05dedaa6ea93bf07194c1ee253126f070bd9d5e1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.13,
          "en": "Now to convert the user finder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.13,
          "end": 6.19,
          "en": "to a class-based component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.19,
          "end": 9.92,
          "en": "I will again import component from React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.92,
          "end": 12.89,
          "en": "and then the final class named user finder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.89,
          "end": 15.493,
          "en": "which extends component of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.62,
          "end": 19.57,
          "en": "Now in here, we need a constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.57,
          "end": 22.6,
          "en": "because we got some state which should be initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.6,
          "end": 25.71,
          "en": "by setting this state to an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.71,
          "end": 29.11,
          "en": "Now here, I actually got two state slices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.11,
          "end": 32.96,
          "en": "the entered search term and then the list of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.96,
          "end": 37.96,
          "en": "and therefore I'll add my filtered users here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.16,
          "end": 41.03,
          "en": "and set that equal to dummy users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.03,
          "end": 43.73,
          "en": "and then add my search term",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.73,
          "end": 46.13,
          "en": "and set this equal to an empty string initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.98,
          "end": 52.53,
          "en": "Next we got a function here to search change handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 57.13,
          "en": "which I'll implement as a method in the user finder clause.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.13,
          "end": 60.41,
          "en": "Because that is then, the function, the methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.41,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "that should be executed to update the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 65.45,
          "en": "At least a part of the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.45,
          "end": 68.35,
          "en": "it should update that search term.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.35,
          "end": 70.39,
          "en": "Now we get to event object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.39,
          "end": 74.09,
          "en": "because this is bound to the change event on the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.09,
          "end": 76.59,
          "en": "and we then use the event object to read",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.59,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "the value entered by the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 81.78,
          "en": "and therefore, we can expect this event object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.78,
          "end": 86.24,
          "en": "as well, to then set our state important here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.24,
          "end": 88.77,
          "en": "always to an object, which is then merged",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.77,
          "end": 92.3,
          "en": "by React and updates the search term part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.3,
          "end": 95.483,
          "en": "of that state to event target value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 97.95,
          "en": "And only that part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.95,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "Again, it will be merged,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 102.253,
          "en": "so the filtered users, won't be lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.86,
          "end": 106.69,
          "en": "Of course, we also need to add a render method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.69,
          "end": 109.27000000000001,
          "en": "where we should return our JS X code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.96000000000001,
          "en": "So grabbed this return statement and add this here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.96000000000001,
          "end": 118.67,
          "en": "In here, I should point at this search change handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.67,
          "end": 122.48,
          "en": "and also to ensure that this keyword works correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.48,
          "end": 127.38,
          "en": "in the method, bind this as explained in the last lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.38,
          "end": 129.9,
          "en": "and here for the filtered users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.9,
          "end": 132.393,
          "en": "we should refer to this .state.filteredusers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.02,
          "end": 138.07,
          "en": "And with that, we transformed this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.07,
          "end": 142.39,
          "en": "At least almost one crucial part is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.39,
          "end": 146.77,
          "en": "and that would be the use effect function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.77,
          "end": 149.513,
          "en": "which we can't use in a class based component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.79,
          "end": 154.15,
          "en": "Now we could derive our filtered users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.15,
          "end": 156.04,
          "en": "and set them in our state update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.04,
          "end": 159.12,
          "en": "here in the search change handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.12,
          "end": 161.19,
          "en": "That would be possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.19,
          "end": 164.35,
          "en": "But I wanna show you how these lifecycle methods work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.35,
          "end": 167.48,
          "en": "and therefore I'll use an alternative approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.48,
          "end": 172.48,
          "en": "We can add component, did update here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.64,
          "end": 177.42000000000002,
          "en": "and this method will be called automatically by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.42000000000002,
          "end": 180.91,
          "en": "whenever this component is re-evaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.91,
          "end": 183.98,
          "en": "because it's state changed, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.98,
          "end": 188.52,
          "en": "So therefore in here we could set our new state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.72,
          "end": 191.283,
          "en": "for the filtered users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.55,
          "end": 194.88,
          "en": "So here we can copy this logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.88,
          "end": 198.01,
          "en": "from the user finder functional component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.01,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "and call this set state to set the filtered users equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.81,
          "end": 206.693,
          "en": "to dummy users filter and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.57,
          "end": 210.23,
          "en": "However, if we want to do it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.23,
          "end": 212.6,
          "en": "we would create an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 212.6,
          "end": 215.72,
          "en": "Because component did update is now executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.72,
          "end": 218.62,
          "en": "every time this component changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.62,
          "end": 221.82999999999998,
          "en": "When we set the state, the component will change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 221.82999999999998,
          "end": 223.87,
          "en": "So then this will execute again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.87,
          "end": 225.75,
          "en": "and it will change the state again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.75,
          "end": 227.6,
          "en": "And it will execute again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.6,
          "end": 230.413,
          "en": "You get my point, this would be an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.44,
          "end": 234.37,
          "en": "Therefore, what we need to do is we need to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.37,
          "end": 237.95,
          "en": "whether the state we're interested in changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.95,
          "end": 241.26,
          "en": "In this case if the search term changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.26,
          "end": 244.24,
          "en": "For that component did update receives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.24,
          "end": 246.37,
          "en": "two arguments which help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 246.37,
          "end": 249.52,
          "en": "The previous props and the previous state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.52,
          "end": 252.42,
          "en": "So the last props and state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.42,
          "end": 255.78,
          "en": "before the current component update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.78,
          "end": 260.78,
          "en": "And with that we can check if prevProps search terms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.83,
          "end": 264.843,
          "en": "with search term was different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.03,
          "end": 269.64,
          "en": "then the current search term.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 269.64,
          "end": 273.98,
          "en": "So this state search term,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.87,
          "end": 278.51,
          "en": "only if it is different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.51,
          "end": 281.47,
          "en": "So only if the search term changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.47,
          "end": 284.15999999999997,
          "en": "I wanna execute this logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 284.15999999999997,
          "end": 287.26,
          "en": "If something else changed, like for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.26,
          "end": 290.11,
          "en": "the filtered users, which we are updating here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.11,
          "end": 294.90999999999997,
          "en": "by calling set state, this method component did update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.90999999999997,
          "end": 298.40999999999997,
          "en": "we'll run again, but we won't make it into this if block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.40999999999997,
          "end": 300.51,
          "en": "So we won't update the state again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.51,
          "end": 303.6,
          "en": "and we won't have an infinite loop, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 307.62,
          "en": "Here by the way, it's not all to be this state search term.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 307.62,
          "end": 310.14,
          "en": "And now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 310.14,
          "end": 315.14,
          "en": "we replace use effect with component did update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 315.81,
          "end": 319.63,
          "en": "This also shows you how nice use effect is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 319.63,
          "end": 324.31,
          "en": "It's very short and by specifying the dependencies here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 324.31,
          "end": 327.29,
          "en": "we don't have to add an if check inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 327.29,
          "end": 329.33,
          "en": "We need to add an if check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 329.33,
          "end": 333.18,
          "en": "for component did update, to prevent an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.18,
          "end": 335.87,
          "en": "but we don't need to do this with use effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 335.87,
          "end": 339.67,
          "en": "because we specified search term as a dependency.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 339.67,
          "end": 343.61,
          "en": "So automatically this affect function will only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 343.61,
          "end": 347.52,
          "en": "be executed by React if that dependency changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 347.52,
          "end": 351.64,
          "en": "And our changes and other reasons for this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 351.64,
          "end": 355.17,
          "en": "to re-render are ignored for this effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 355.17,
          "end": 357.8,
          "en": "because of this dependencies array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 357.8,
          "end": 359.9,
          "en": "Now, one thing I just noticed by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 359.9,
          "end": 363.82,
          "en": "of course I don't wanna compare prevProps, but prevState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 363.82,
          "end": 367.68,
          "en": "The previous state search terms should be compared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 367.68,
          "end": 370.9,
          "en": "If you would be updating based on prop changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 370.9,
          "end": 372.79,
          "en": "So you got some new prop values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 372.79,
          "end": 375.68,
          "en": "and you wanna add the component there for updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 375.68,
          "end": 378.93,
          "en": "then you could compare previous props to current props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 378.93,
          "end": 382.22,
          "en": "but here it's the state change, which matters to us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 382.22,
          "end": 384.67,
          "en": "the state change inside of this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 384.67,
          "end": 387.62,
          "en": "and hence we compare our previous state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 387.62,
          "end": 391.66,
          "en": "a specific slice of that state with the current state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 391.66,
          "end": 393.873,
          "en": "and that specific slice of that state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 395.03,
          "end": 398.45,
          "en": "Now we should also add super in the constructor by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 398.45,
          "end": 402.86,
          "en": "before we forget this, and now we transformed this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 402.86,
          "end": 405.02,
          "en": "and we can hence remove user finder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 405.02,
          "end": 408.633,
          "en": "in the functional forum or simply comment it out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 409.7,
          "end": 414.7,
          "en": "And now if I go back this again, works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 416.32,
          "end": 419.15,
          "en": "but now with class-based components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 419.15,
          "end": 421.54,
          "en": "and component did update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 421.54,
          "end": 425.2,
          "en": "And as I mentioned before in this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 425.2,
          "end": 427.58,
          "en": "it's a different mental model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 427.58,
          "end": 430.51,
          "en": "When you work with these lifecycle methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 430.51,
          "end": 435.51,
          "en": "you primarily think about when will this method be called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 435.56,
          "end": 438.38,
          "en": "Which is the case when the component updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 438.38,
          "end": 440.62,
          "en": "And then you might need to add if checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 440.62,
          "end": 444.49,
          "en": "to restrict your logic in there with use of fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 444.49,
          "end": 445.67,
          "en": "you don't care about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 445.67,
          "end": 448.58,
          "en": "whether the component is rendered for the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 448.58,
          "end": 451.29,
          "en": "or if it updated or whatever, you care about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 451.29,
          "end": 453.7,
          "en": "the fact that search term changed.",
